The purpose of the adjustments made on May 10, 2017, as per Article 16 - Job Vacancies, was:

- To stay competitive in the labour market;
- To attract external applicants, as job titles were being misunderstood;
- To ensure sufficient CA (Certified Apprentice) or supervisory coverage per WorkSafe requirements;
- To comply with BC Safety Authority requirements by having Chief Engineers at each location.

These adjustments were made under Article 16 - Job Vacancies, specifically section 16.04, and included removing “and Leadhands” from the heading and rewording the language regarding how job vacancies for trades and leadhands are filled — to clarify the criteria for hiring based on seniority, qualifications, and ability.

The adjustments were negotiated between the BC Tree Fruits Cooperative (Employer) and United Food and Commercial Workers International Union, Local 247 (Union).

The purpose of the adjustments made on May 10, 2017, as per Article 16 - Job Vacancies, was to:

- Clarify and correct job title misunderstandings in the marketplace to attract external applicants;
- Ensure adequate CA (Certified Apprentice) or supervisory coverage in compliance with WorkSafe requirements;
- Meet BC Safety Authority requirements by mandating the presence of Chief Engineers at each location.

These adjustments were made under Article 16 - Job Vacancies, specifically subsection 16.04, to improve clarity in job vacancy procedures for trades and leadhands, including rewording the language to better reflect the intent and requirements for filling such positions.

